  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns 480. I worked it out by hand and got the same result when I ran the function.\n\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = 600.\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` takes off 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 480.\n\n`service2` only imports `pricing` and `discounts`. Nothing imports `decoy_tax.py` (its gold rate is 25) or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
